\begin{slide}
Exercises\\
1. Rewrite equation \eqref{cblerreq}
\[\cblerreq\]
to show the terms in the canonical order with position error, velocity error, and then attitude error.

2. Determine the $7^\text{th}$ row of the system matrix $F$ for the canonical 9-state error model.  Use the cross-product operator matrix as required, e.g.,
$\rotmat{I}{E}^L=\xop{\omega_{IE}^L}=\xopdef{\left[\omega_{IE}^L\right]}$.  Introduce simplifying notation!  E.g., set $\alpha=\omega_{IE}^L$  Hint:  Use telescope pointint angle error equation \eqref{telscopeeq}
\end{slide}
